WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.962
CUBE goes beyond ROLLUP by returning every grouping
combination for the listed

00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:10.650
dimensions With category and product CUBE produces
four analytical levels First

00:00:10.788 --> 00:00:16.325
category and product together Second category totals
across all products

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.162
Third product totals across all categories Fourth
the grand total across everything

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:29.375
That product-only subtotal is the important
difference from the ROLLUP example ROLLUP

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.012
follows one hierarchy CUBE explores all combinations
The query

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:39.350
again uses GROUPING inside CASE expressions so
subtotal placeholders can be labeled

00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:44.950
clearly The grouping_code helps identify which
dimensions are active in each row

00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:49.800
Run the query and compare it with the previous slide
You should

00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:54.512
see more subtotal rows because CUBE adds the
product-only level CUBE can

00:00:54.538 --> 00:00:59.325
be useful in multidimensional reporting but it can
grow quickly With more

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:05.025
dimensions the number of grouping combinations
increases substantially That can make both

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:09.650
the result and the computation larger Use CUBE when
the report truly

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:14.238
needs all combinations If you only need a few
specific summary levels

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.562
GROUPING SETS is usually more controlled
